# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Every blob in this repository is LF, but Git's Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.  That breaks the one
# verification a reader is asked to perform: re-run a producer and compare its
# output with the committed aggregate.  The producers write LF, so on a stock
# Windows clone every artifact compares as modified even though the JSON is
# identical -- a phantom diff that reads like the release does not reproduce.
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout match the blob everywhere, which is also
# what the per-cell JSONL should be: they are data, not source for a compiler.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
